module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Noetherian
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Immersion
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.ImmersionStalk
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Koszul.MinimalGenerators

/-!
# Regular sequences in a factorization of a regular immersion

Let `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` be immersions of schemes with `X` locally Noetherian, and
suppose the composite `i ≫ j` is a regular immersion.  Stacks tag 09RK concludes that `i` and
`j` are themselves regular immersions.  Because `X` is locally Noetherian, regularity may be
tested on local rings, so the content of 09RK at a point `z : Z` is the pair of statements that
the kernels of

* `O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Y, i z}`, and
* `O_{Y, i z} ⟶ O_{Z, z}`

are generated by regular sequences.  This file proves exactly that pair, from the regular
sequence generating the kernel of the composite — which
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.ImmersionStalk` supplies — together with the
injectivity of the induced map of cotangent spaces, which is the conclusion of Stacks tag 09PV.

## Main results

* `Koszul.exists_isRegular_ker_of_injective_mapQ_of_surjective`: the ring-theoretic core.  For a
  surjection `φ : A → B` of commutative rings with `A` Noetherian local and a further ring map
  `ψ : B → C`, if `ker (ψ ∘ φ)` is generated by a regular sequence and the induced map of
  cotangent spaces `ker φ / 𝔪 ker φ → ker (ψ ∘ φ) / 𝔪 ker (ψ ∘ φ)` is injective, then `ker φ` is
  generated by a regular sequence of `A` and `ker ψ` is generated by a regular sequence of `B`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors`:
  the same statement for the two maps of local rings attached to a factorization of a morphism
  of schemes through two immersions over a locally Noetherian base.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf`
  `.exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors_of_isRegularIdealSheaf`: the previous result
  with the regular sequence for the composite supplied by the regular ideal sheaf of the
  composite, which is the form Stacks tag 09RK is stated in.

## Implementation notes

The ring-theoretic core is a corollary of
`Koszul.exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_of_injective_mapQ_maximalIdeal`
(Stacks tag 09PW without its first hypothesis), which concludes that `ker (ψ ∘ φ)` *maps* to a
regularly generated ideal of `A ⧸ ker φ`.  Surjectivity of `φ` is what turns that quotient into
`B` itself: the first isomorphism theorem gives `A ⧸ ker φ ≃+* B`, this isomorphism carries the
image of `ker (ψ ∘ φ)` onto `ker ψ` because `ker (ψ ∘ φ) = φ⁻¹ (ker ψ)` and `φ` is surjective,
and a regular sequence transports along a ring isomorphism by `AddEquiv.isRegular_congr`.

Surjectivity of the stalk maps is where the immersion hypotheses enter: `IsImmersion` extends
`IsPreimmersion`, which is `SurjectiveOnStalks` together with injectivity on points.  Only the
surjectivity of `j`'s stalk maps is used; `i`'s immersion hypothesis is carried because 09RK
assumes it and because it is what makes the composite an immersion.

The injectivity hypothesis is *not* proved here.  It is the conclusion of Stacks tag 09PV, whose
Stacks proof goes through Gulliksen's method (tag 09PU) and Tate resolutions (tag 09PN); neither
of those tags has a carrier in this library.  Taking it as a hypothesis isolates it as the one
remaining input, in exactly the shape
`Koszul.exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_of_injective_mapQ_maximalIdeal`
consumes.  Note that the cotangent map is written with `Submodule.inclusion` applied to a
specific proof of the inclusion of ideals; since that argument is a proof of a proposition, any
other proof of the same inclusion gives the same map.

The main result takes the regular sequence generating the kernel of the composite as a bare
existential statement about the local ring, which is the weakest form and is what both results
of `…ImmersionStalk` produce.  The corollary supplies it from a regular ideal sheaf on `X`
itself; that is the hypothesis shape of `exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap`, and it is
*stronger* than the hypothesis Stacks 09RK uses, which asks only that the defining ideal sheaf
be regular on the canonical open on which the composite is closed.  Supplying `hreg` from that
weaker hypothesis goes instead through `exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_of_generators`,
whose data is already purely local, together with a transport of regular generators from the
open subscheme to `X`; that transport is not proved here.

No Stacks tag attribute is carried by any declaration in this file.  Tag 09RK asserts that `i`
and `j` *are* regular immersions unconditionally; the results here carry the 09PV conclusion as
a hypothesis, so none of them states 09RK, and none states 09PW either, whose first hypothesis
is finite tor dimension rather than injectivity on cotangent spaces.  The tag belongs on
whichever declaration eventually discharges that hypothesis.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 37.62.11 (Tag 09RK)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RK)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 23.9.5 (Tag 09PW)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PW)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 23.9.4 (Tag 09PV)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PV)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory
open AlgebraicGeometry
open RingTheory.Sequence

universe u

namespace Koszul

open IsLocalRing Submodule

/-- The kernel of a ring map is contained in the kernel of any further composition with it.

Mathlib has this for linear maps (`LinearMap.ker_le_ker_comp`) and has both halves of it for
ring maps (`Ideal.ker_le_comap` and `RingHom.comap_ker`), but not the composite statement; it is
named here because it appears inside the statement of the results below, as the argument of
`Submodule.inclusion`. -/
theorem ker_le_ker_comp {A B C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    (φ : A →+* B) (ψ : B →+* C) : RingHom.ker φ ≤ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ) :=
  (Ideal.ker_le_comap (K := RingHom.ker ψ) φ).trans (RingHom.comap_ker ψ φ).le

/-- **Stacks 09PW, in the shape a factorization supplies.** Let `φ : A → B` be a surjection of
commutative rings with `A` Noetherian local, and let `ψ : B → C` be a further ring map.  If the
kernel of `ψ ∘ φ` is generated by a regular sequence of `A` and the induced map of cotangent
spaces `ker φ / 𝔪 ker φ → ker (ψ ∘ φ) / 𝔪 ker (ψ ∘ φ)` is injective, then the kernel of `φ` is
generated by a regular sequence of `A` and the kernel of `ψ` is generated by a regular sequence
of `B`.

The injectivity hypothesis is the conclusion of Stacks tag 09PV. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_ker_of_injective_mapQ_of_surjective
    {A B C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Nontrivial B] [Nontrivial C]
    (φ : A →+* B) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (ψ : B →+* C)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A (RingHom.ker φ))).mapQ
        (maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A (RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ))))
        (Submodule.inclusion (ker_le_ker_comp φ ψ))
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ _)))
    (hreg : ∃ rs : List A, IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) :
    (∃ rs : List A, IsRegular A rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker φ) ∧
      (∃ qs : List B, IsRegular B qs ∧ Ideal.ofList qs = RingHom.ker ψ) := by
  obtain ⟨hI, qs, hqs, hqsJ⟩ := exists_isRegular_ofList_eq_of_injective_mapQ_maximalIdeal
    (RingHom.ker φ) (RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) (RingHom.ker_ne_top φ)
    (RingHom.ker_ne_top (ψ.comp φ)) (ker_le_ker_comp φ ψ) hinj hreg
  set e := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hφ with he
  refine ⟨hI, qs.map e, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine (AddEquiv.isRegular_congr (e := e.toAddEquiv) ?_).mp hqs
    refine List.forall₂_map_right_iff.mpr (List.forall₂_same.mpr ?_)
    intro q _ x
    exact map_mul e q x
  · have hmap : (Ideal.ofList qs).map (e : A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ →+* B) = Ideal.ofList (qs.map e) :=
      Ideal.map_ofList _ qs
    rw [← hmap, hqsJ, Ideal.map_map]
    have hcomp : (e : A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ →+* B).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker φ)) = φ := by
      ext x
      rfl
    rw [hcomp, ← RingHom.comap_ker ψ φ, Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective φ hφ]

end Koszul

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

open IsLocalRing Submodule

/-- **The local-ring content of Stacks 09RK.** Let `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` be immersions of
schemes with `X` locally Noetherian, and let `z : Z`.  If the kernel of the map of local rings
induced by `i ≫ j` is generated by a regular sequence and the induced map of cotangent spaces is
injective, then the kernels of the two maps of local rings in the factorization are generated by
regular sequences.

The injectivity hypothesis is the conclusion of Stacks tag 09PV applied to the nested ideals
`ker (j.stalkMap (i z)) ⊆ ker ((i ≫ j).stalkMap z)` of `O_{X, j (i z)}`. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors
    {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (z : Z)
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))).mapQ
        (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker ((i.stalkMap z).hom.comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))))
        (Submodule.inclusion
          (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (i.stalkMap z).hom))
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ _)))
    (hreg : ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))),
      IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker ((i ≫ j).stalkMap z).hom) :
    (∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))),
        IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom) ∧
      (∃ rs : List (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)),
        IsRegular (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom) := by
  have hcomp : ((i ≫ j).stalkMap z).hom
      = (i.stalkMap z).hom.comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]
    rfl
  rw [hcomp] at hreg
  exact Koszul.exists_isRegular_ker_of_injective_mapQ_of_surjective
    (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (j.stalkMap_surjective (i.base z)) (i.stalkMap z).hom hinj hreg

/-- **Stacks 09RK at a point, with the composite's regular sequence supplied by its regular ideal
sheaf.** If the defining ideal sheaf of `i ≫ j` is a regular ideal sheaf and the map of cotangent
spaces at `z` is injective, then the kernels of the two maps of local rings in the factorization
are generated by regular sequences. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors_of_isRegularIdealSheaf
    {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j]
    [IsImmersion (i ≫ j)] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (z : Z)
    (h : IsRegularIdealSheaf X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom (i ≫ j)))
    (hz : (i ≫ j).base z ∈
      idealQuotientSupport X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom (i ≫ j)))
    (hinj : Function.Injective
      ((maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))).mapQ
        (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker ((i.stalkMap z).hom.comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))))
        (Submodule.inclusion
          (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (i.stalkMap z).hom))
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ _))) :
    (∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))),
        IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom) ∧
      (∃ rs : List (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)),
        IsRegular (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom) :=
  exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors i j z hinj
    (exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap (i ≫ j) h z hz)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
